      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T14:25:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we perhaps relax this? I think the HAL\u0027s client (keystore) will and should continue providing the auth token and timestamp token on every call for simplicity, but I wonder if we should actually specify that. Implementers might assume that this means HAL service implementations must also provide those tokens on every call, but for contexts where comms between the AP and the secure environment are slow (eSEs, basically), it might make sense for the HAL service to be smarter and to avoid sending tokens when it knows the secure side has already checked them and cached the result.",
